WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.840
We are here with the incomparable Marie Osmond.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.470
And I happened to be with your brother,

3
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:13.330
and it's funny, 'cause we talked about some deep stuff.

4
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.989
Really? He's not that deep.

5
00:00:14.989 --> 00:00:16.840
(Drew laughing)

6
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.160
Well, that's going to lead perfectly into our game,

7
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.880
Donny versus Marie.

8
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.253
And we asked him some questions.

9
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.180
And now we're going to ask you in a game we're calling,

10
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.916
Donny versus Marie.

11
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:31.926
(upbeat music)

12
00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:33.192
Oh, no.

13
00:00:33.192 --> 00:00:36.225
(audience clapping)

14
00:00:36.225 --> 00:00:37.750
All right.

15
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.910
Okay, here's how it works.

16
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.320
I'm going to ask you a question

17
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.480
and after you answer, we'll see what Donny said.

18
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.990
And if you can match three out of five of Donny's answers,

19
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:49.840
you win.

20
00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.250
And if you win,

21
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.380
Donny said, he'll go on his Instagram

22
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.150
and sing "Paper Roses," your iconic hit song.

23
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.160
But if you lose,

24
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.730
apparently you have agreed to go on your Instagram

25
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.949
and sing "Puppy Love," his iconic song.

26
00:01:07.949 --> 00:01:08.840
(Marie laughing)

27
00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.041
Okay.

28
00:01:10.041 --> 00:01:13.210
This is making it nerve wracking and more exciting.

29
00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.510
In other words, I have to win.

30
00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.423
Okay. Gotcha.

31
00:01:16.472 --> 00:01:19.193
Okay. Here we go.

32
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.513
Number one,

33
00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:24.780 line:15%
who is more likely to forget the lyrics to a song?

34
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.613 line:15%
Me.

35
00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.530 line:15%
Here's what Donny said.

36
00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.303 line:15%
So Marie is going to say it's me,

37
00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:32.683 line:15%
but it's Marie.

38
00:01:34.055 --> 00:01:35.297 line:15%
(bell ringing)

39
00:01:35.297 --> 00:01:36.130
Okay.

40
00:01:39.091 --> 00:01:41.924
No, it's me. It's definitely me.

41
00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:43.693
All right.

42
00:01:43.693 --> 00:01:47.400 line:15%
Who doesn't mind re-wearing costumes without being cleaned?

43
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.320 line:15%
He would probably say me.

44
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.233 line:15%
All right. Donny's answer was.

45
00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.468 line:15%
That's definitely me.

46
00:01:54.468 --> 00:01:55.676 line:15%
(buzzer buzzing)

47
00:01:55.676 --> 00:01:56.509 line:15%
Yeah, it's him.

48
00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:57.800 line:15%
He's right. It is him.

49
00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.864
Okay.

50
00:01:58.864 --> 00:02:00.820
I got that one wrong. Okay.

51
00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.610
We're one for one here. All right.

52
00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:07.393 line:15%
Who is likely to eat food after it fell on the floor?

53
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:09.783 line:15%
Donny.

54
00:02:10.749 --> 00:02:11.990 line:15%
(audience laughing)

55
00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.910 line:15%
And Donny's response was.

56
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.992 line:15%
Oh, that's definitely Marie.

57
00:02:16.992 --> 00:02:19.120 line:15%
(buzzer buzzing)

58
00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.480 line:15%
She has the three second rule.

59
00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.583
Actually, she pushes it to 10 seconds.

60
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.050
I thought this is where we could bond,

61
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.408
'cause I have the same rule.

62
00:02:29.408 --> 00:02:30.980
He's kind of weird.

63
00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.460
Yeah that's okay, I'll give him that one.

64
00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.950
Okay.

65
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.200 line:15%
Who was the favorite growing up?

66
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.830 line:15%
Donny.

67
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.400 line:15%
And Donny's response was.

68
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.233 line:15%
Me.

69
00:02:41.233 --> 00:02:43.960 line:15%
Marie is going to say it was her, but it was me.

70
00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.500 line:15%
All right, you get that one.

71
00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.110
(audience clapping)

72
00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.197
We're two to two.

73
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.072
Okay.

74
00:02:52.072 --> 00:02:54.923
I'm just going by what I know his brain would say.

75
00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.720
It was me.

76
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.450
All right. Well, this is the tie breaker.

77
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.263 line:15%
Who is more likely to keep a secret?

78
00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.670 line:15%
Well, it's me, but he'll say it's him.

79
00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.050 line:15%
Well, here's what Donny said.

80
00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.190 line:15%
Me,

81
00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:17.210 line:15%
because I told her I was the peacock

82
00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.053 line:15%
on "The Masked Singer,"

83
00:03:18.053 --> 00:03:19.380 line:15%
He's so full of crap.

84
00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.546 line:15%
And she let it out.

85
00:03:20.546 --> 00:03:23.213 line:15%
(Drew laughing)

86
00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.520
Is that true?

87
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:29.150
Did yo tell people he was "The Masked Singer?"

88
00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.640
So, he told me because he was flying in and out.

89
00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.150
And then I was doing some press,

90
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.211
I can't remember what project I was doing,

91
00:03:37.211 --> 00:03:40.630
and their network people,

92
00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:41.890
they said, "oh yeah how about that?

93
00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:43.340
You know, Donny is the peacock."

94
00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:46.420
They set me up and I went, "oh, I guess they told him

95
00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.880
because it's the network."

96
00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.170
And I said, "oh yeah, right."

97
00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.640
And then I realized they'd set me up

98
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.650
and then I tried to get out of it.

99
00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.720
Oh, he was so mad.

100
00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.460
Oh my gosh, he was so mad. (laughing)

101
00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.310
I love that that was the answer.

102
00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:01.084
We all jumped for joy when Donny was doing that.

103
00:04:01.084 --> 00:04:01.917
So what does this mean?

104
00:04:01.917 --> 00:04:04.550
This means he's singing "Paper Roses," right?

105
00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.140
It means he is singing "Paper Roses," Marie.

106
00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.384
Okay, I'm watching.

107
00:04:09.384 --> 00:04:10.217
All right.

108
00:04:10.217 --> 00:04:13.600
And then I'll give you my response on my social media.

109
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.517
And that means you win.

110
00:04:15.517 --> 00:04:19.820
Marie's newest album "Unexpected" is out now.

111
00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.930
And also her latest special "An Evening With Marie"

112
00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.540
on BYU TV is out.

113
00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:26.800
Please enjoy it.

114
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.150
Thank you so much, Marie.

115
00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.254
Thank you.

116
00:04:29.254 --> 00:04:31.837 line:15%
(upbeat music)

